# CompTIA A+ — Hardware

Which RAM form factor do most laptops use?
---
SODIMM
~ DIMM
~ SIMM
~ CAMM
---
Small Outline DIMM, about half the length of a desktop DIMM.

How many pins does a DDR4 desktop DIMM have?
---
288
~ 240
~ 260
~ 184
---
DDR3 DIMMs have 240. DDR5 also uses 288 but is keyed differently.

Which RAM type detects and corrects single-bit memory errors?
---
ECC
~ Dual-channel
~ SODIMM
~ Registered
---
Error-Correcting Code memory, common in servers and workstations.

Which interface gives an NVMe SSD its speed?
---
PCIe
~ SATA
~ USB
~ SAS
---
NVMe drives talk PCIe directly, skipping the SATA bottleneck of about 600 MB/s.

Which SSD option is the fastest?
---
NVMe
~ SATA M.2
~ mSATA
~ 2.5-inch SSD
---
Same slot as SATA M.2, different protocol. Check the key notch and the board manual.

Which RAID level mirrors two drives with no striping?
---
RAID 1
~ RAID 0
~ RAID 5
~ RAID 10
---
RAID 0 stripes for speed with no redundancy. RAID 5 stripes with parity across three or more drives.

How many drives does RAID 5 require at minimum?
---
3
~ 2
~ 4
~ 5
---
One drive's worth of capacity goes to parity. RAID 10 needs four.

Which CPU socket type puts the pins on the motherboard?
---
LGA
~ PGA
~ BGA
~ ZIF
---
Land Grid Array, used by Intel desktop sockets. PGA puts pins on the chip. BGA is soldered down.

What does the CPU use thermal paste for?
---
Filling air gaps between the CPU and heat sink
~ Gluing the heat sink in place
~ Insulating the CPU electrically
~ Lubricating the fan bearing
---
Air is a poor conductor. The paste fills microscopic gaps so heat reaches the sink.

Which power connector feeds a modern GPU?
---
PCIe 8-pin
~ Molex 4-pin
~ SATA 15-pin
~ EPS12V 8-pin
---
Often 6+2 pin. High-end cards take two or three, or the newer 12VHPWR.

Which motherboard form factor is the smallest of the standard three?
---
Mini-ITX
~ microATX
~ ATX
~ E-ATX
---
170 mm square, one expansion slot. microATX sits between it and full ATX.

What is the first laser printer imaging step?
---
Processing
~ Charging
~ Exposing
~ Cleaning
---
The full order: processing, charging, exposing, developing, transferring, fusing, cleaning.

Which printer type uses a thermal print head and special paper?
---
Thermal
~ Laser
~ Inkjet
~ Impact
---
Receipt printers. The paper darkens with heat, and fades with time and sunlight.

Which printer type can print multi-part carbon forms?
---
Impact
~ Laser
~ Inkjet
~ Thermal
---
Dot matrix pins physically strike the ribbon, so the impact carries through the copies.

What does a UPS provide that a surge protector does not?
---
Battery power during an outage
~ More outlets
~ Faster charging
~ Grounding
---
An Uninterruptible Power Supply bridges outages long enough to save work and shut down cleanly.
